    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0546" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg438"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Señor
                            Cayetano Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your notes of 12th instant and to say that I have communicated to the
                    Secretary of War the suggestion that the U. S. Government station troops at the
                    fords of the Rio Grande between Rio Grande City and Laredo, and also the
                    statement which you send me relative to the Mexican forces now on the right bank
                    of that river.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
